==============================================================================================================
REPORTED: ownership classes, UFD link, constants, extension cost
==============================================================================================================
  class E (GCs, wide binaries): they sit inside the host's full-rank sigma_c -> f = 1 at their positions. The switch cannot make them
    Newtonian; that needs the ownership rule unchanged (CFG333 R2, FG001 formation classes: no own cold clump -> no own phantom). The
    literal 'outermost bound system owns the phantom' would ALSO strip satellite dSphs (class A) of their own phantom, so the working
    rule is R2, which the switch neither supplies nor breaks.
  class A dwarfs: own cold clump, full rank -> ON (consistent).
  UFD link: CFG344 assumed CDM-like cold structure; an exactly cold phase-space sheet (needed here for (a)) clusters down to small scales,
    UFD clumps are full rank -> ON; consistent (the same coldness assumption serves both).
  constants: R-3 0, R-3s 0 (beyond kappa = 1/2). Extension cost: B's cold component becomes a full phase-space (Vlasov) sheet, not dust;
    the 10-moment closure cannot create rank (congruence), so the kinetic caustic step is required; exact primordial coldness is required (A4).

